     <!--#include virtual="/php/suttasidebar.html" --> 

  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="thag12.1" class="h1">Thag 12:1  Sīlavat</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>Here master the virtue</p>
              <p>that in this world is well-mastered,</p>
              <p>for virtue, when cultivated,</p>
              <p>brings every consummation near.</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Wise, one should protect one’s virtue,</p>
                <p>aspiring to three pleasures:</p>
                <p>praise, the gaining of wealth,</p>
                <p>and—after death—rejoicing in heaven.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>The virtuous one, through restraint,</p>
                <p>acquires many friends,</p>
                <p>while the unvirtuous one, practicing evil,</p>
                <p>from friends is estranged.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>The unvirtuous person gains</p>
                <p>disrepute &amp; dishonor;</p>
                <p>the virtuous person, always,</p>
                <p>repute, honor, &amp; praise.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Virtue is the beginning, the establishing,</p>
                <p>the mother of what is fine,</p>
                <p>the foremost of all qualities:</p>
                <p class="v2">Therefore virtue should be purified.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Virtue is also control, restraint,</p>
                <p>the delight of the mind,</p>
                <p>the ford of all Buddhas:</p>
                <p class="v2">Therefore virtue should be purified.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     an incomparable strength.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     the ultimate weapon.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     the highest adornment.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     an astounding coat of mail.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     an imposing bridge.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     an unexcelled fragrance.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     the highest fragrant ointment</p>
                <p class="v7">by which one wafts</p>
                <p class="v7">this direction &amp; that.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     the supreme provision.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     the ultimate food for the journey.</p>
                <p class="v1">Virtue:     the highest vehicle</p>
                <p class="v7">by which one goes<span class="fn"><a href="#thag12.1note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
                <p class="v7">this direction &amp; that.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Right here he gains blame,</p>
                <p>and after death, in deprivation,</p>
                <p>he’s unhappy at heart:</p>
                <p>Everywhere the fool</p>
                <p>is unhappy at heart,</p>
                <p>not concentrated on virtues.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Right here he gains honor</p>
                <p>and after death, in heaven,</p>
                <p>is happy at heart:</p>
                <p>Everywhere the enlightened one</p>
                <p>is happy at heart,</p>
                <p>well-concentrated on virtues.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Here virtue is supreme,</p>
                <p>but one with discernment is the ultimate.</p>
                <p>Among human beings &amp; devas</p>
                <p>one conquers</p>
                <p>through virtue &amp; discernment.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="thag12.1note01">1. Reading <em>yāti</em> with the PTS and Sinhalese editions. The Thai has <em>vāti</em>—“wafts”—which seems to be a mistake.</p>
            </div><!--end notes-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
